  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=EX6-006#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for EX6-006 (Sep. 6, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you must delete them.",
        "question": "Do I have to delete all of my Digimon for this card's [Start of Your Main Phase] effect even when I have 0 cards in my Digi-Egg deck and can't place a card in digivolution cards?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, they are.  When cards such as [Leviamon] and [Leviamon (X Antibody)] differ in that one has [X Antibody] and the other doesn't, you can reference the cards as if they have different names.",
        "question": "If [Leviamon] and [Leviamon (X Antibody)] are in this card's digivolution cards, are they considered \"cards with different names\"?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it does.",
        "question": "Does [Gate of Deadly Sins] itself in digivolution cards also count for this card's \"if this Digimon has 5 or more digivolution cards with different names\"?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, that's correct.",
        "question": "If multiple copies of this card are in digivolution cards, does its inherited effect overlap?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can choose not to.",
        "question": "Do I have to activate this card's inherited effect when a Digimon card would be played?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, that's correct.",
        "question": "Can I also activate this card's inherited effect when a Digimon would be played by an effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's inherited effect to reduce the digivolution cost by 3 even if this card has 5 or more digivolution cards with different names?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
